{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-79793",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2$, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4)\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
